			],
			"Message": "chore(Wind): Remove obsolete backlink comment from NotificationStream.ts\n\nDelete the temporary backlink reference `Backlink: Land/.claude/tauri/Patches/14-StreamingGRPC.md (P14.5)` that was added as a documentation artifact during the Vine notification stream implementation. This comment served as an implementation reference during development but is not needed in the final module documentation.\n\nThe module header comment explaining the reference-counted Tauri channel behavior is preserved.",
			"SHA": "c095ad3e7a3843944cb662083b5595007a2011b8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T02:18:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1035,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Vine notification stream service\n\nImplement `VineNotifications` and `VineNotificationsLive` - an Effect-TS Layer that bridges Mountain's process-wide Vine notification broadcast to a `Stream<NotificationFrame>` consumable by Wind/Sky subscribers.\n\nThe Layer opens a Tauri channel via `vine_subscribe_notifications` command, draining the Mountain broadcast receiver into an unbounded Effect Queue. It wraps this in the `VineNotifications` service tag so consumers can `yield*` the stream and use Effect-TS operators like `Stream.filter`, `Stream.runForEach`, and `Stream.merge`.\n\nAlso adds:\n- `SubscribeMethodPrefix` and `SubscribeMethod` convenience functions for filtering\n- `SubscriberCount` diagnostic to query Mountain's active subscription count\n- Proper acquireRelease bracket ensuring the Rust drain task exits when the Layer goes out of scope\n\nRef: Land/.claude/tauri/Patches/14-StreamingGRPC.md (P14.5)",
			"SHA": "274df239ea812e7a2db00cabae032cf152210ecd"
		}
	],
